Scope held to the two files; nothing staged or committed. Every N got its failing test first — the eight new r3 deftests produced 17 red assertions against the r2 code (all other 40 tests stayed green) before the fixes.

## Per-finding disposition

| Finding | Disposition |
|---|---|
| **N1** (P1 regression: the 10⁶ bound gave the judge a silent finite lifetime) | **Fixed per the reviewer's scheme.** `magnitude-limit` = 2⁵² replaces `magnitude-bound` in `duration?`/`tolerance?` (raw bound); a new division-based `base-over-bound` joins the universal shape gate — `n > (quot magnitude-limit unit-magnitude)` for a unit the supplied table knows — so every product ≤ 2⁵² and every sum ≤ 2⁵³ on all three hosts, while an ms reading stays legal ~140,000 years. `check-units!` bounds table magnitudes at 2⁵². `apply-tick-value` now **counts** a structurally defective tick in `:dropped` — a rejected tick is a signal, never a silent no-op. Tests: `r3-tick-past-the-old-bound-advances-now-test` (a `{s 4000000000}` tick advances `now`, and the arithmetic still orders a `:cap` at that scale), `r3-over-bound-reading-is-a-structural-defect-test` (per-unit by division: `{:s 4503599627370497}` and even raw-legal-but-per-unit-over `{:s 4503599627370496}` defective; `{:s 4503599627370}` legal), `r3-over-bound-unit-table-refused-test` (over-2⁵² magnitude refused; `{:ms 1 :h 3600000}` legal again), `r3-over-bound-tick-on-tick-cursor-is-visible-test` (counted, `now` unchanged, no abort). Existing bound-pinning tests re-based (`{:ms 1000001}` now asserted *legal*, hostile corpus entry moved to 2⁵²+1). |
| **N2** (P2-4 relocated, not fixed) | **Fixed.** `:answered` is keyed `[proposer proposal-id]`. The hook shape is now `{:grants [grant-fact...] :refusals [{:proposer author :refusal fact}...]}` — a grant answers the proposal of the holder it carries (proposer derivable outright), while a refusal names no proposer of its own, so the hook supplies the proposal's author it refuses; documented in `initial-judge`'s and `answer-and-grant`'s docstrings. `deliver-authored`/`flush-queue`/`apply-authored` thread the proposer; the drain gate derives it (holder for grants, nil otherwise); a drained refusal echo records no answer (documented — its repeat protection is the delivery gate). Test: `r3-two-holders-sharing-a-proposal-id-test` — B's refused `:p1` does not block A's `:p1`: both answers delivered, A's grant seeds, `:dropped` 0. Corpus and answer-hook tests re-keyed to proposers. |
| **N3** (grant registration switched off the unregistered fallbacks) | **Fixed.** Only holder-authored facts register (eligible renewal or release); the self-authored-grant clause is gone — a drained grant seeds tenure but claims no medium. Test: `r3-grant-drained-then-holder-medium-truncated-test` — grant drained from a cursor, holder's medium truncated before any renewal: no silence lapse; once the drain reaches quiescence the never-renewed lease does lapse (and the writer holds only the record — a drained grant was never written to it). |
| **N4** (`:tolerance` never validated) | **Fixed.** `initial-judge` throws at assembly on a non-`tolerance?` shape or a unit outside the table (docstring states why: a foreign-unit tolerance would throw from `add-duration` mid-pass, after step 3 already delivered grants). Test: `r3-tolerance-validated-test` (four bad shapes refused; zero and nil accepted). |
| **N5** (catch-all turned an exception wedge into a silent permanent abort; `Throwable`) | **Fixed.** Value processing is extracted into `process-fact-value` and wrapped per element: a throw there **drops that element, advances the cursor past it, counts it in `:dropped`, and continues**. A throw from the read itself still aborts as `:dao.stream/transport-error`, now with the message under `:abort-error`, and all catches take `Exception` under `:clj` (never `Throwable`), the host-appropriate type elsewhere. The false "no cursor is left wedged" claim is corrected in the `drain-ticks`, `drain-facts` and `judge-step` docstrings, which now state both behaviors. Test: `r3-resolver-throw-drops-element-and-continues-test` (resolver throwing on a poisoned envelope: element dropped, clean renewal after it applied, no abort). `r2-thrown-read-folds-into-abort-test` still pins the throwing-read case. |
| **N6** | **No code change**, per disposition — the orchestrator has the §6 row ("the grant declares its medium", Phase 4). |

